We add $\goldD{\dfrac{225}{4}}$ inside the parentheses, and subtract $\greenD{1}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{225}{4}}$ outside them, to keep the expression equivalent.

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\greenD{} \left(x^2 +15 x\right) +54
\\\\
&=\greenD{}\left(x^2 +15 x+\goldD{\dfrac{225}{4}}\right) +54 -\greenD{1}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{225}{4}}
\\\\
&= \left(x +\dfrac{15}{2}\right)^2 +54 -\dfrac{225}{4}
\\\\
&= \left(x +\dfrac{15}{2}\right)^2 -\dfrac{9}{4}
\end{align}$
